---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Help with the Golden Moments App"
  seoTitle="App Help: Gentle Games and Family Photos"
  description="Help for the Golden Moments app: start a gentle game, change comfort settings, add family photos, play offline and remove copies safely."
  path="/help/"
  crumb="App help"
  updated="2026-10-25"
  lede="Start small, follow the person’s interests and stop whenever you like."
>
  <aside class="notice" aria-labelledby="help-version">
    <div>
      <strong id="help-version">Check your version first</strong>
      <p>
        These steps describe version 1.4.0 and later. Earlier versions have different screens and do not include family
        photos. Update from the <a href={SITE.appStoreUrl} rel="noopener">App Store</a> or
        <a href={SITE.playStoreUrl} rel="noopener">Google Play</a> when the update is offered.
      </p>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <h2>Start a gentle game</h2>
  <p>
    Choose <strong>Start a gentle game</strong>. The first board has four large tiles with the pictures showing. Tap two
    pictures that match. There is no timer, score or penalty. Choose <strong>Done for now</strong> whenever you want to
    stop.
  </p>

  <h2>Adjust the pictures</h2>
  <p>
    Open <strong>Comfort settings</strong> to change the number of tiles or whether pictures stay showing. The choices
    depend on how many pictures there are. Your settings are saved on this device, and you can go back to a smaller
    board at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Add family photos</h2>
  <p>
    Open <strong>Your family photos</strong>, then <strong>Choose photos</strong>. Pick only photos you may use and that
    the person is comfortable seeing. The app keeps smaller copies of up to 24 photos. It does not scan the rest of your
    library or change your originals.
  </p>
  <p>
    Add at least two photos for a matching game, or choose <strong>Look at photos together</strong> to enjoy them one at a
    time. Optional conversation prompts have no right answer. Simply looking together is enough.
  </p>

  <h2>Play offline</h2>
  <p>
    All eight picture packs come with the app, so they need no downloads. Photo copies work offline once added. If an
    original is stored only in iCloud or another cloud photo service, your device may need the internet to fetch it
    while you add it.
  </p>

  <h2>Remove a copy safely</h2>
  <p>
    Open a photo’s <strong>Options</strong> and choose <strong>Remove this copy</strong>, or choose
    <strong>Remove all photo copies</strong>, and read the message before you confirm. This removes the app’s copies, not
    the originals in your photo library. There is no photo sync or transfer to another device. Device backups may
    include app data, depending on your settings. <a href="/privacy-choices/">More about removing copies</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
  <p>
    If choosing photos is cancelled, try again when you are ready. If adding photos fails, keep your originals and try
    fewer photos. If a screen is stuck, close and reopen the app. Do not delete the app or clear its storage as a first
    step: that can remove saved copies and settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    If photos or settings seem to be missing, stop making changes and <a href="/support/">contact support</a>. Tell us
    your device, its system version, the app version and what happened. Please do not send family photos, passwords or
    medical details.
  </p>

  <h2>Comfort comes first</h2>
  <p>
    Offer choices rather than asking someone to remember a name or finish a board. Change the picture or stop if it
    feels uncomfortable. Golden Moments offers enjoyment and conversation; it does not diagnose, measure, treat or
    prevent dementia or Alzheimer’s disease. Read more in <a href="/safety/">safety and intended use</a> and
    <a href="/caregiving/how-to-play-together/">how to play together</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
